# Continuation of our own model happens through nep.restart, which
# round1.5_nep.sbatch copies in from round1_out/dataset. GPUMD's fine_tune
# keyword is only for the 89-element foundation model, so it is not used.
#
# --- architecture: MUST match round1_nep-1.in exactly, or round 1's -------
# --- nep.restart cannot be continued (the parameter vector would be a  ----
# --- different length). Copied verbatim from round1_nep-1.in.          ----
type          3 N Al Si # this is a mandatory keyword
version       4       # default
cutoff        6 4     # default
zbl           2
n_max         12 8     # default
basis_size    12 12     # default
l_max         4 2 0   # default
neuron        60      # default

# --- loss weights: carried over unchanged from round1_nep-1.in. Note that ---
# --- lambda_f 50 against lambda_e 0.1 makes forces ~500x more important   ---
# --- than energies; round 0's energy RMSE never came down as a result.    ---
lambda_e      0.1     # default
lambda_f      50     # default
lambda_v      0.1     # default
batch         1000    # default
population    50      # default

# --- generation: continuing from round 1's restart needs far fewer than  ---
# --- a from-scratch run. Watch round1.5_out/round1.5_loss-1.out: round 0 ---
# --- reached its best test force RMSE around generation 20000 and got    ---
# --- worse after that, so consider cutting this down.                    ---
generation    200000  # default
